valstr=0,Rules
valstr=1,Initial Setup
valstr=2,Content Changes

[enum_3372]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
outputstring=yes
defaultstr=null
valstr=0,Your character starts outside Lumbridge Castle.|Your character begins restricted to the areas of Misthalin and Karamja. As you complete tasks, you can unlock more areas.|Full information about each of the areas can be found in the Area Selection Menu. This can be accessed from the Leagues Menu in the Journal Panel.|All experience gained will be multiplied by 5x, and this will increase as you unlock more Relics.|Content released during Leagues V will be reviewed and enabled for the League on a case-by-case basis.|Leagues V: Raging Echoes will run from November 27th 2024 until the game update on January 22nd 2025.
valstr=1,Your character is an Ironman, meaning you cannot trade with other players.|As you begin with Misthalin and Karamja unlocked, the following quests have been auto-completed:|- Dragon Slayer<br>- Druidic Ritual<br>- Elemental Workshop I<br>- Bone Voyage<br>    - Dig Site<br>- Fairytale II - Cure a Queen<br>   - Fairytale I - Growing Pains<br>      - Lost City<br>      - Nature Spirit<br>         - Priest in Peril<br>         - The Restless Ghost<br>- Shilo Village<br>   - Jungle Potion|You will start with the following stat increases:|- 3 Herblore<br>- 5 Runecraft|A Dramen Staff will be added to your Inventory so that you can access Zanaris. If lost, you can reclaim it from the Sage in Lumbridge.<br><br>Any pets obtained in the previous league can be freely reclaimed from the Sage or Probita. Pet transmogs you may of obtained in the previous league will also be auto unlocked at the start of the league, though these will both no longer count towards your collection log total counter on a league world.
valstr=2,Slayer Masters will assign you the same tasks, taking into account the areas you have currently unlocked.|Teleports and transportation methods to locations outside of areas you have unlocked are restricted.|When purchasing your Player Owned House it will be accessible from Brimhaven. Your house can only be moved to areas you have unlocked.|Unlocking new areas will complete various quests and Achievement Diary tasks but will not award any quest completion XP. However, you may complete some quests on your own to gain their XP before unlocking the area which auto-completes it.|Some bosses will have the option to be fought in private areas without other players.|Some shop items will have infinite stock and let you buy items already noted.|The following shop stocks have been modified:|- Pestle and Mortars and Box Traps have been added to the Lumbridge General Store<br>- Black Platelegs have been added to Horvik's Armour Shop<br>- Elemental Shields have been added to all Slayer Equipment shops|Thessalia in Varrock will offer additional makeover services.|Impling spawn rates have been increased.|Rarity of rare implings has been increased.|Dragon implings drop reduced Dragon Bones.|All Soulreaper Axe pieces will drop from every Desert Treasure 2 Boss.

[enum_3373]

[enum_3374]

[enum_3375]

[enum_3376]

[enum_3377]
inputtype=struct
outputtype=boolean
default=1

[enum_3378]
inputtype=int
outputtype=boolean
default=1

[enum_3379]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
outputstring=yes
defaultstr=Welcome to Leagues V - Raging Echoes!
valstr=0,Welcome to Leagues V - Raging Echoes!
valstr=3,The Leagues Menu
valstr=4,The Leagues Menu
valstr=5,Tasks
valstr=7,Areas
valstr=9,Relics
valstr=11,Finishing Up

[enum_3380]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
outputstring=yes
defaultstr=
valstr=0,<col=ffffff>Leagues</col> are time-limited <col=ffffff>game modes</col> that give you new ways to experience the world of <col=ffffff>Gielinor</col>.<br><br>The aim of each <col=ffffff>League</col> is to complete <col=ffffff>tasks</col> and earn<br><col=ffffff>League Points</col>. These <col=ffffff>points</col> can then be exchanged for various <col=ffffff>unlocks</col> and <col=ffffff>rewards</col>.<br><br>To begin your journey in <col=ffffff>Leagues V</col>, use the<br><col=ffffff>Get Started</col> button below. Otherwise, you can use the<br><col=ffffff>Exit Leagues</col> button to quit.
valstr=3,In <col=ffffff>Leagues V</col>, progression is key. To help you keep track of it, you have the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col>. This is an extra section to the <col=ffffff>Journal Panel</col> whilst on a <col=ffffff>Leagues World</col>.<br><br>Let's open the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col> now. To do so, look for the flashing <col=ffffff>quest icon</col> on your screen.
valstr=4,Now that you have your <col=ffffff>Journal Panel</col> open, you can open the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col>. To do so, look for the flashing <col=ffffff>Leagues tab</col>.
valstr=5,Congratulations, you've completed your first <col=ffffff>task</col> in<br><col=ffffff>Leagues V</col>!<br><br>Completing <col=ffffff>tasks</col> is the ticket to success in any <col=ffffff>League</col> as doing so earns you <col=ffffff>League Points</col>.<br><br>Let's take a look at the <col=ffffff>task list</col> now. To do so, look for the flashing <col=ffffff>tasks button</col> in the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col>.
valstr=7,In <col=ffffff>Leagues V</col>, the world of <col=ffffff>Gielinor</col> is split up into different <col=ffffff>areas</col>. Most of these have been locked off, but you can unlock new ones by completing <col=ffffff>tasks</col>.<br><br>Now that you've completed your first <col=ffffff>task</col>, you can unlock a new <col=ffffff>area</col>! To do so, look for the flashing <col=ffffff>areas button</col> in the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col>.
valstr=9,Completing <col=ffffff>tasks</col> doesn't just give you access to new <col=ffffff>areas</col>. The <col=ffffff>League Points</col> you earn from completing them can be used to unlock powerful <col=ffffff>Relics</col>!<br><br>Let's take a look at these <col=ffffff>Relics</col> now. To do so, look for the flashing <col=ffffff>Relics button</col> in the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col>.
valstr=11,You are now ready to properly start your adventure in <col=ffffff>Leagues V - Raging Echoes</col>!<br><br>If you need a recap on anything, you can use the <col=ffffff>info button</col> in the <col=ffffff>Leagues Menu</col> at any time. Alternatively, the<br><col=ffffff>Sage</col> in <col=ffffff>Lumbridge</col> can provide you with some<br>useful guidance.<br><br>When you are ready to begin, just use the <col=ffffff>End Tutorial</col> button below to get started.

[enum_3381]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
outputstring=yes
defaultstr=
valstr=0,Exit Leagues
valstr=11,End Tutorial

