[enum_5722]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
outputstring=yes
defaultstr=null
valstr=0,Your character starts outside Lumbridge Castle.|Your character begins restricted to the areas of Misthalin and Karamja. As you complete tasks, you can unlock more areas.|Full information about each of the areas can be found in the Area Selection Menu. This can be accessed from the Leagues Menu in the Journal Panel.|All experience gained is heavily increased, and this will further increase as you unlock more Relics.|Content released during Leagues V will be reviewed and enabled for the League on a case-by-case basis.|Combat Masteries offer customizeable combat power, earnt via various milestone challenges.|Each area has an Echo Boss, these are enhanced bosses that pose a challenge and drop new unique rewards, you can kill the regular boss to get an Echo Orb that lets you access the Echo variant, more information can be found in the area interfaces.|Leagues V: Raging Echoes will run from November 27th 2024 until the game update on January 22th 2025.
valstr=1,Your character is an Ironman, meaning you cannot trade with other players.|You will start off with Misthalin and Karamja unlocked, with everything those areas provide you.|You will start with the following stat increases:|- 3 Herblore<br>- 5 Runecraft|A Dramen Staff will be added to your Inventory so that you can access Zanaris. If lost, you can reclaim it from the Sage in Lumbridge.
valstr=2,Slayer Masters will assign you the same tasks, taking into account the areas you have currently unlocked.|Teleports and transportation methods to locations outside of areas you have unlocked are restricted.|When purchasing your Player Owned House it will be accessible from Brimhaven. Your house can only be moved to areas you have unlocked.|Unlocking new areas will complete various quests and Achievement Diary tasks but will not award any quest completion XP. However, you may complete some quests on your own to gain their XP before unlocking the area which auto-completes it.|Most shop stock will not deplete.|The following shop stocks have been modified:<br>- Elemental Shields have been added to all Slayer Equipment shops|Impling spawn rates have been increased.|Rarity of rare implings has been increased.|Dragon implings drop reduced Dragon Bones.|All Soulreaper Axe pieces will drop from every Desert Treasure 2 Boss.|Pets and any pet transmog items that roll over between leagues do not count towards the collection log tasks.|The Twisted Bow, Scythe of Vitur, and Tumeken's Shadow are available from all three raids.|Items that drop as components that require multiple regions to create a usable item will drop as the finished item.|CoX: CM, ToB: HM and ToA 500+ have significantly buffed drop rates and difficulty, ToA and ToB will now provide uniques to all players in the raid if the raid obtains one.|Pet Transmogs will now roll over between leagues.|The Sage can sell Max Capes once you are eligible.|Nihil Shards drop in increased quantity from Nex.|Players can access Tormented Demons without WGS completed.|Scythe of Vitur can be charged with just blood runes.|Zulrah has no damage cap or melee damage immunity.|Forestry Events are three times as likely to spawn.|Wilderness Bosses can be accessed without the Wilderness Medium Diary.

